# Byte-exact test fixtures must always be checked out with LF endings:
# the wire-protocol golden transcripts are compared byte-for-byte
# against the Go encoder's "\n"-terminated output, so CRLF conversion
# would fail them on Windows with core.autocrlf=true.
*.golden text eol=lf

# Go source is always LF: gofmt on Windows flags CRLF as a full-file
# diff (every line removed+re-added), which masks real formatting issues
# and makes CI's gofmt check unreliable. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working
# treeLF regardless of core.autocrlf, so `gofmt -l` reports only genuine
# formatting drift — required for the v0.6.0 test-coverage/quality gate.
*.go text eol=lf

